Octave Blocks 0.3.0

Adds cached compiled acceleration, flat adaptive C export, Transport Delay,
Limited Integrator, programmatic modeling and recorded Simulink evidence.
The combined distribution is GPL-3.0-or-later to include adapted Octave
solver components, with solver attribution and generated-code notices;
original MIT notices remain in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

Uses GNU Octave package conventions: inst/ for installed functions,
inst/private/ for shared implementation, doc/ for documentation, and
DESCRIPTION, COPYING and INDEX for package installation and discovery.
Examples are installed separately from the public API in inst/examples/.
Tests and benchmarks remain in tests/ and are not added by pkg load.
Advanced simulation is integrated into this layout.

New Simulink library builders, built from native primitives so that
ob_run, zero crossings, strict C99 ob_codegen and ob_accelerate all work,
with Simulink's defaults, validateattributes-style 'ob_<name>:' errors,
and regression suites checked against recorded Simulink 26.2 traces:

 ** Nonlinear and logic: ob_backlash, ob_quantizer, ob_minmax,
    ob_saturation_dynamic, ob_dead_zone_dynamic, ob_sign,
    ob_coulomb_viscous_friction, ob_relational_operator and
    ob_logical_operator (n inputs from two-input chains, NXOR, vectors).
    Relational and Logical Operators output double 0/1.

 ** Routing and sources: ob_mux and ob_demux (any number of inputs, declared
    widths), ob_multiport_switch (control truncated toward zero, as
    Simulink records it), ob_pulse_generator and ob_chirp.

 ** Continuous and multirate: ob_second_order_integrator,
    ob_first_order_filter, and ob_rate_transition, which builds Simulink's
    Integrity/Deterministic Rate Transition modes between explicit rates.

New analysis functions ob_linearize (linmod), ob_findop (trim), ob_bode
(frequency response, margin/allmargin) and ob_stepinfo (stepinfo), checked
against Simulink 26.2 linmod/trim and Simulink traces.

The Simulink-style command API maps the new blocks by their Simulink R2026b
library paths and built-in/<BlockType> names (Backlash, Quantizer, MinMax,
Saturation Dynamic, Sign, Dead Zone Dynamic, Coulomb & Viscous Friction,
Relational and Logical Operator, Multiport Switch, Pulse Generator,
including sample-based pulses, Chirp Signal, Mux, Demux and
Integrator, Second-Order), and sim() accepts SaveFormat 'Dataset': yout and
the Scope logsout become Dataset-like structs with numElements,
getElement, get and getElementNames, recorded against Simulink 26.2. The
model default stays 'Array'. The handles survive Octave's binary/text
save and load; for MAT files, remove them and rebuild the Dataset with
ob_simulink ('dataset', s). A Mux or Demux signal whose shape differs
from the declared width stops sim with an error that names the block.
Rate Transition library blocks accept Integrity and Deterministic; with
an explicit OctaveInputSampleTime (an Octave Blocks extension) they map
onto ob_rate_transition. Without it only the default (both on) is
accepted, as the native sample-and-hold; setting either to off is an
error.

Other changes:

 ** Linux fixes: accelerated models no longer read each other's tables
    when several are loaded in one session (MEX symbols are now hidden
    outside Windows); generated C builds warning-free with glibc and gcc
    15; ob_run reports ob_run:ode15sUnavailable when Octave was built
    without SUNDIALS IDA. tests/run-tests-linux.sh runs the test stages
    on Linux.

 ** ob_accelerate falls back to a temporary cache directory when the
    per-user cache is not writable, and accelerator load failures name
    the cache and suggest setting OB_ACCELERATOR_CACHE.

 ** The Qt editor test stage (tests/Test-Editor.ps1) fails fast with an
    explanation instead of hanging in session 0 or behind Octave's
    first-run welcome wizard.

 ** Project branch names are neutral and documentation references are
    current.

 ** NEWS is now the single changelog; the former CHANGELOG.md entries are
    folded in below.

Not added: Zero-Order Hold (use a native Rate Transition), Moving Average,
Bus Creator/Selector (use ob_mux/ob_demux), sample-time reports and model
diagnostics.

See doc/README.md for the documentation index.


Octave Blocks 0.2.1-preview.1

 ** Adopts GNU Octave package layout and metadata for pkg install and
    pkg load.

 ** Groups shared internals under inst/private/, public functions under
    inst/, and runnable examples under inst/examples/.

 ** Folds the compiler-only multiple-output shape helper into its caller.

 ** Moves guides and project records into doc/, with a documentation
    index.

 ** Adds installable .tar.gz archives alongside source ZIPs in release
    packaging.


Octave Blocks 0.2.0-preview.1

Source preview of the merged event-export milestone.

 ** Public C99 RK4 export for supported primitive and continuous-control
    events.

 ** Shared parent/child continuous stages, clocks and input callbacks.

 ** Transactional C APIs with failure and rollback checks.

 ** Input lookup, graph, numeric formatting and editor improvements.

 ** README images, analytical oscillator example, contribution guide and
    source-release packaging.

Requires a separate GNU Octave installation; verified on Octave 11.3.0 on
Windows. Does not include the accelerator or reorganization in draft PR #4.
Adaptive C solvers, arbitrary Octave-to-C translation and Simulink file
interchange remain outside this release.

See doc/VALIDATION.md for recorded milestone evidence and
doc/COMPATIBILITY_GAPS.md for remaining work.
